# Mosaic theologian

Offline study assistant: a general local chat model plus a local index of Scripture, this church's belief statements, and its sermon transcripts. Questions are embedded at ask time. The model is not fine-tuned on the church.

Windows (`Mosaic-NightJob.ps1`) crawls, transcribes, and indexes. The Intel Mac (`mosaic.sh`) only verifies the copied bundle and asks. `lib/` and `query/` ship in the bundle so both machines run the same retrieval and prompt.

Authority order: Scripture, then belief statements, then sermons and articles, then general knowledge under its own heading. If the church has not addressed the question, say so. A passage marked `Connected in` a sermon is that sermon's link, not Scripture citing Scripture.

Before describing the project, porting it, or changing crawl, index, retrieval, prompting, or export, read `.cursor/skills/mosaic-theologian/SKILL.md` and follow it.

Do not break these:

- Resume safety is write order: artifact on disk, then job step. `*.part` plus rename. A kill may cost one item. Do not rely on catching Ctrl+C.
- Sermon identity is the normalized audio URL, not the page URL.
- Reject a Bible source with fewer than 66 books. Never commit verse text (`data/bible/` stays gitignored).
- The embedding model, revision, and dimension in the index manifest must match the model that queries. A mismatch is a hard stop. Changing the embedding model requires a full reindex.
- Keep collections `scripture`, `beliefs`, and `mosaic` separate and weighted. Publish a reindex only when the side index is complete.
- Night-job order drains on-disk audio first; index must not block crawl or download. Abort a crawl on HTTP 429 or 403.
- Bind the chat server and web UI to loopback, and keep the query runtime hub-offline.
